      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Microplastics",
                "marks": [
                  {
                    "type": "bold"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Microplastics are pieces of plastic smaller than five millimetres. Some are manufactured at this size, such as the tiny beads once common in cosmetics, while others form when larger items break down. Scientists have found microplastics almost everywhere they have looked: in oceans, in Arctic ice, in drinking water and even in human blood."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Several countries, including the UK and the USA, have banned microbeads in rinse-off cosmetics. However, researchers point out that these beads represent only a small share of the problem. A much larger source is synthetic clothing: every time polyester or nylon is washed, thousands of tiny fibres are released."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The effects on human health are not yet clear. Laboratory studies suggest that high concentrations may damage cells, but the amounts people are exposed to in daily life may be far lower. Most experts agree that more research is needed before firm conclusions can be drawn."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "attrs": {
          "start": 10
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Microplastics are pieces of plastic smaller than five millimetres. (T/F/NG)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
